From ba48779cac04ad3578d46ccd84c31ab315719fdc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: askimi <44218719+RNI4114@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 16:02:24 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 03/10] jay: halt in a divergent loop body reconverges
 physically at the loop exit

jay_block_reconverge() adds the physical (UGPR) edges of a halt only to the
convergence blocks in converge_blocks, but the innermost one lives in
nj->converge_block and is only pushed there when a nested if/loop is
entered. A halt directly in the body of a divergent loop therefore had no
physical edge to the loop exit, although the lanes that broke out of the
loop resume there in the same thread right after the halting lanes are
disabled.

RA could then reuse UGPRs that are live in the code after the loop. In a
raytracing resume shader that ends a loop iteration with trace_ray + halt,
the trace block overwrote the stack IDs copied from r1 that the
btd_retire after the loop uses, so the wrong stacks were released while
their rays were still in flight. Stacks got reused, return addresses were
overwritten and threads spawned garbage shader records: GPU hang in
Cyberpunk 2077 path tracing (a shadow ray loop with SkipClosestHit, which
puts lanes from different iterations in the same resume thread).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 5e42eb1da1e2bd944632905681f25d20ae57e24c)
(cherry picked from commit e23249efcf9477712b8cc4380234e8112524539f)
---
 src/intel/compiler/jay/jay_from_nir.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/intel/compiler/jay/jay_from_nir.c b/src/intel/compiler/jay/jay_from_nir.c
index c9d4a600ead..e3e4738cef2 100644
--- a/src/intel/compiler/jay/jay_from_nir.c
+++ b/src/intel/compiler/jay/jay_from_nir.c
@@ -3741,6 +3741,17 @@ jay_block_reconverge(struct nir_to_jay_state *nj,
           */
          jay_block_add_successor(current_block, *conv, UGPR);
       }
+
+      /* The innermost convergence point is not in converge_blocks, it is only
+       * pushed there when entering a nested if/loop. Without this edge a halt
+       * directly in a divergent loop body (e.g. the trace_ray + halt that ends
+       * a raytracing resume shader inside a loop) does not physically fall
+       * through to the loop exit, where the lanes that broke out of the loop
+       * resume, so RA may clobber UGPRs that are still live there (the stack
+       * IDs of btd_retire, which then releases the wrong stacks).
+       */
+      if (nj->converge_block)
+         jay_block_add_successor(current_block, nj->converge_block, UGPR);
    } else {
       assert(!jump);
       jay_block_add_successor(current_block, after_block, GPR);
